# Build output. `cargo test -p labwired-core --test e2e_nrf52840_obd2_scanner`
# produces this directory itself; nothing in it is committed.
#
# These rules live HERE and not inside build/, because the Makefile's `clean`
# does `rm -rf $(BUILD_DIR)`: a .gitignore in there is deleted by the first
# clean, and the object files it was hiding then land in the next `git add -A`.
# That is not hypothetical -- it happened, and binaries reached a commit.
build/
